## Design Rationale

Explain class selection, responsibility allocation and key relationships.

The three classes chosen were Patient, Practitioner, and Appointment because it keeps the system simple, and sorts the tasks into three different sections. The Patient class is responsible for all the Patient user interactions and verifying them to then be passed onto another class, this is because the Patient could input incorrect data. The Practitioner class is responsible for updating the Practitioner’s availability, and verifying that an appointment is allowed, as the Practitioner’s schedule is extremely important to include. The Appointment Class is responsible for the functions of booking, updating, cancelling, and displaying the list of appointments. This is extremely important to the project because the main goal of the program is to manage and track appointments.

